137	// failure occurs after enforceModelRPS has already incremented the counter, so that
138	// requests which never reached the backend do not consume quota.
139	// Note: if the 1-second window expires between the increment and this decrement, the
140	// decrement lands on a fresh (zero) key and drives the counter negative. Preventing this
141	// would require an atomic floor-at-zero Lua script, which is not worth the added complexity
